00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.554
In this episode, we're going to talk about electronic locks.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.490
So why did we come to Korea to film this?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.791
Because, do you know that

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.927
the reason electronic locks have developed on a large scale worldwide

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.362
is

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.263
because of Korea?

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.832
This factory is basically the master of electronic locks.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.100
Basically, from the time

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.468
you saw

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:38.338
oppas in Korean dramas more than 40 years ago, pressing the electronic lock so coolly

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.106
and being able to enter

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.474
in style, to the present day,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.609
we can use fingerprints

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.977
, visual recognition

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.311
, or palm vein

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.446
recognition

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.281
. This factory has made a great contribution to all of this.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.383
You'll find that it's the Korean factory behind me. The sheer number of Taiwanese women

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.385
who have built up the entire electronic lock industry

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.186
is astonishing.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.222
So, on this day,

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.958
which happens to be zero degrees Celsius

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.293
, we made a special trip to South Korea

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.595
to film an electronic lock company.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.997
Besides electronic locks, this episode

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.799
will also discuss a way to make money. According to statistics,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.700
the penetration rate of electronic locks

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.002
in South Korea

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.970
is around 98%,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.105
while in Taiwan it

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.206
's less than 30%

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.508
. That means over 70% of the money-making opportunities

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.810
lie in electronic locks.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.911
But have you ever wondered

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.713
why, even though electronic locks are so widespread in South Korea

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.215
, many Taiwanese people still don't install them

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.416
, or don't want to replace them?

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.018
They often lose their keys , frequently need to call a locksmith

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:25.919
, or often can't open their doors.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.454
It turns out that many people

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.755
have a very negative impression

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.989
of electronic locks;

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.424
Taiwanese people don't like installing them.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.625
There are four main reasons why electronic locks

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.793
are so prone to failure. First, they are expensive.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.095
Second, they often run out of power , requiring

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.929
battery replacements

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.763
or becoming unusable.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.597
Third,

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.899
many people find that electronic locks break down easily after installation.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.501
Fourth, and most importantly,

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.236
besides the high price of locks

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.538
, Taiwan has a wide variety of door sizes,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.573
which contributes to

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.475
the high cost of replacing electronic locks.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:51.077
However, you can

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.378
find the answers to these questions

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.447
by watching this episode . Why did early electronic locks break down so easily?

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.149
Because the evolution of electronic locks

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.017
to the present day is roughly 40 years

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.353
old. Over 40 years ago, they were basically operated by entering passwords

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.721
or using cards.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.922
Think about it:

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.258
40 years ago, many things didn't

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.860
exist. There was no national

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.995
health insurance, no GPS... PS

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.363
didn't have smartphones

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.898
40 years ago, nor did it have democracy.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.199
So, in just 40 years,

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.168
you can see how many new things

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.169
and technologies have developed

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.904
. Its technology has evolved step by step.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.340
Although many people mistakenly believe that

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.609
many components are imported from mainland China,

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.744
or that visual recognition is

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.412
synonymous with facial recognition and

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.414
Chinese devices,

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.116
have you ever wondered

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.652
why many people don't use facial recognition?

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.554
Because facial recognition raises personal data concerns.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.257
And why has facial recognition technology developed so well in China?

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:37.857
Because

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.758
the Party needs it,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.226
the Party needs your face.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.294
So, regardless,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.096
let's go into the factory and see

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.964
how this electronic lock works. This is how they did it.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.367
The largest electronic lock factory in South Korea,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.636
a factory comprised of a group of South Korean middle-aged women

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.605
, can change the entire South Korean electronic lock market. Just

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.707
how big and amazing is this production line?

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.644
It can produce more than 3,000 electronic locks a day! That

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.279
's how big it is,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.113
unbelievable!

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.614
How amazing are these South Korean middle

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.516
-aged women? One out of every two electronic locks in South Korea

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.351
is made by them.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.319
If you

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.087
've ever wanted to replace your electronic lock

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.355
, or if you find electronic locks convenient

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.890
but don't understand their structure,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.692
then in this episode, I will try my best

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.893
to explain the principles of electronic locks to the general public

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.662
in a way that you can understand,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.130
and how to choose an electronic lock.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.865
First, stand in

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.966
the center of me.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.734
Imagine me as... One door

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.502
after another,

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.071
electronic locks will definitely have front-opening and back-opening

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:25.939
options.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.473
When choosing an electronic lock,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.708
you don't need to listen to a lot of

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.776
jargon about

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.811
how great it is or what functions it has.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.646
You can explain it into three main categories:

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.648
how to open, how to pull,

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.749
and how to lock. What does "how to open" mean

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.017
? It refers to how

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.285
an electronic lock opens.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.453
Nowadays, there are many functions:

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.588
fingerprint unlocking,

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.789
Wi-Fi unlocking

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:43.890
, password unlocking

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.492
, card unlocking , and

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.227
recently popular

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.161
visual recognition like facial

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.529
and palm vein recognition.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.197
The second option is how to pull.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.298
Whether you're opening or closing,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.299
you need to pull the door.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.567
There are several

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.368
ways to pull

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.136
: one is like a traditional horn lock,

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:57.870
and another... So ,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.872
the third type is the 90-degree rotating handle,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.540
and

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.741
the second type is

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.743
the pull-pull type.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.477
How do you pull it?

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.778
The third type is how to lock it.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.814
Actually, the third type is the most important of all.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:10.149
That's why we went to a factory in Korea to film

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.352
this – the most important thing is how to lock it.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.688
If

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.489
you

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.957
're not a locksmith,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.425
you usually won't see this.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.660
The most important

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.295
part of an electronic lock is the lock cylinder

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:23.229
. The lock cylinder's structure

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.564
is actually very simple.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.532
We can use a 3D diagram to show you.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.834
The lock cylinder

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.535
is installed on your door panel.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.570
When the door panel

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.472
is opened or closed,

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.339
this thing

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.674
touches your door, and

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.743
it senses the door... Once it's closed,

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:37.810
it will automatically lock.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.212
Or, when

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.880
you're opening it, the latch—

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.748
this latch

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:42.548
, this bean curd—

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.650
is on your tongue.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.151
How smoothly

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.252
it opens and closes

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.321
depends entirely on

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.122
the

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.690
quality of the basic hardware and industrial processing

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.658
.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.093
So why do I say the third point, how to lock,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.628
is the most important? Because

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.363
locking a door,

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.066
you know, a door lock is a door.

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:00.767
If a door can't be locked,

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.435
what's the

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.436
point of having a door

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.203
?

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:04.904
So, does that make sense

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:05.271
?

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.239
Now, if I have Wi-Fi,

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:06.806
visual recognition,

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:07.907
fingerprint, and palm vein recognition

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:08.975
, I can pull and push the door like a mansion door,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:09.876
automatically locking after someone leaves.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:10.510
The door won't lock

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.711
in two seconds

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.547
, so many people use exaggerated

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:15.882
features like "what functions it has" to

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.650
describe it . But the most important thing is that it's

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.020
like a car with a beautiful

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:21.721
interior , lots

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.722
of trim panels, and

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.190
built-in navigation—

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.224
what's the use

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.159
if the engine breaks down?

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.327
So, I think

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:28.528
many people want to buy an electronic lock

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.196
, but the first thing you should care about is

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.864
where the lock cylinder is made.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:32.965
That's

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:33.766
the key

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.735
. Now that you have these three basic concepts—

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.003
how to open

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.738
, how to pull, and how to lock—

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:39.906
we can look at

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.307
how an electronic lock is installed

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.809
. First, what kind of components do you need to install

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:43.676
? Let's

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.111
go to

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.280
the small parts area at the very beginning

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.550
of the factory . First, we need to install the door handle. The door

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.018
handle looks like this.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.653
If you want to add a function

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.489
, you need to add a small component,

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.091
like a

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.692
fingerprint sensor

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.361
. If you want to add a fingerprint sensor

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.162
to your door handle,

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.365
the first thing is to make an opening

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.232
during injection molding.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.000
Then, you need to install the

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.502
fingerprint

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.436
electronic component.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.537
This way, when you push the door handle,

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.272
your fingerprint can be pressed.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.607
So, it's back to

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.142
the present day... Adding one more part

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.143
means one more expense,

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.412
and adding one more part means one more electricity consumption.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.080
So let's start

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.049
assembling our door handle.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:23.449
Well...

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.250
speaking of which...

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.118
adding one more part

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.319
means one more electricity consumption.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.587
Let's install our handle.

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:27.920
Huh?

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.788
You didn't get it?

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:29.555
I didn't get it?

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:32.225
Adding one more part means one more electricity consumption,

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:32.925
a little bit

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.593
more electricity,

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.560
and then it's all about the handle.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.329
The handle is

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.764
too subtle, isn't it?

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:38.931
Let's install the handle.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.783
In a short moment,

00:06:56.783 --> 00:07:00.052
the Korean aunties have already formed their own production line

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.254
. In fact, every single one of them,

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.822
every single one of them, they all

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.123
know how to do it . So they're like

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.491
a guerrilla force now

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.827
. When they find something stuck at the back,

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:09.829
they run to the front. When they find something stuck at the front, they start locking it.

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.097
Now they start automatically gluing it.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.098
From

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.433
beginning to end,

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.668
no foreman or supervisor has come to talk to them.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.270
They haven't said a word. They've

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.772
all been aligning themselves with their bodies.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:20.940
From the moment they started assembling until now,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.108
they haven't said a word.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:23.176
So now, you see in front of me,

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.111
a whole row of very cute

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.979
array-style production lines has appeared

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.714
at this station. There's a small detail

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.683
you can see. Look at our second auntie.

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:34.454
In front of her, where she's tightening the screws, there's a machine .

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:35.555
That machine is called

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:37.457
KILEWS. KILEWS

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:40.193
is an automatic screw feeder.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.962
Its internal structure is simple and interesting.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.831
Previously, when tightening screws,

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:46.365
you'd pick up a screw,

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:48.868
then use a screwdriver or drill

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.036
to tighten it

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.204
. So, for each part,

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.639
you had to pick up a screw from a bunch, align

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:54.407
the Phillips head

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:56.075
with the screwdriver, and then tighten

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.477
it – very cumbersome.

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:59.412
But with KILEWS, it 's

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:00.313
different.

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.381
When you open it, there's a scoop inside.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:03.983
It scoops up the screw, and

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:05.384
due to

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.420
gravity, it falls to the middle,

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.187
like a row of

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.755
screws forming a bridge.

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:12.024
There's a broom-like mechanism that keeps

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.593
sweeping . The principle is that

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:14.694
if the screw threads

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.028
aren't on the bottom,

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.029
it will be swept away, and

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:17.830
the

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.931
screws on the bottom

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.099
will be inserted into the feeder.

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:23.302
Finally, it's fed out from the outlet at the front.

