She's an old hand,

00:15:55.888 --> 00:15:56.689
didn't succeed

00:15:56.689 --> 00:15:57.423
. Sister.

00:15:57.423 --> 00:15:58.857
Is that right?

00:15:58.857 --> 00:16:00.559
You're pretty.

00:16:01.527 --> 00:16:03.195
What should I say...

00:16:03.195 --> 00:16:04.463
I love you, sister.

00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:09.368
No, although I find it annoying.

00:16:09.368 --> 00:16:12.538
But because he's so handsome, I can't bring myself to curse him.

00:16:12.538 --> 00:16:14.273
Look, it's slowly accumulating here,

00:16:14.273 --> 00:16:16.041
and lunchtime is almost here.

00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:17.009
Look, it's

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:21.647
12:30 now. It stopped as

00:16:21.647 --> 00:16:22.548
soon as

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:26.352
 

00:16:26.352 --> 00:16:27.820
it hit 30, and then they left

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:29.655
for lunch.

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:31.290
I thought they'd

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.325
eat like that Korean Minister Kim,

00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:34.360
and then rush off

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:35.494
. The older women

00:16:35.494 --> 00:16:36.261
are

00:16:36.261 --> 00:16:38.097
quite reserved

00:16:38.097 --> 00:16:40.432
. What do Korean older women eat?

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:43.969
I followed them

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:47.873
to a small eatery. Hey,

00:16:47.873 --> 00:16:49.174
a Korean small eatery

00:16:58.017 --> 00:16:59.985
... this reminds me of the one I ate when I was little...

00:16:59.985 --> 00:17:01.487
Han Il-gwan, do you remember it?

00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:03.555
Han Il-gwan Korean BBQ

00:17:03.555 --> 00:17:05.224
... They need

00:17:05.224 --> 00:17:07.026
soup in this

00:17:07.026 --> 00:17:08.427
... Oh, they need soup in this...

00:17:08.427 --> 00:17:09.161
Sorry,

00:17:09.161 --> 00:17:10.496
I didn't know

00:17:12.464 --> 00:17:13.732
... I don't know ...

00:17:13.732 --> 00:17:15.000
I'm..." "Hai" What?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.201
This is Korea.

00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:17.503
This is how Taiwanese people put things.

00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:20.372
The proper way to put things in Korea is like this.

00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:21.073
And do you

00:17:21.073 --> 00:17:22.775
know how much a whole plate like this

00:17:22.775 --> 00:17:23.809
costs?

00:17:23.809 --> 00:17:25.844
6500 Korean won,

00:17:25.844 --> 00:17:27.813
150 NT dollars. It's all-you-can-eat

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:29.548
, meaning if you get hungry in the middle,

00:17:29.548 --> 00:17:31.917
it's a gift from the Korean lady. Oh,

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:34.119
it's a gift from the Korean lady

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:35.454
. Thank you,

00:17:35.454 --> 00:17:36.755
I'm so happy.

00:17:36.755 --> 00:17:40.959
(Ten minutes later)

00:17:40.959 --> 00:17:42.795
They eat super fast, so rushed!

00:17:42.795 --> 00:17:44.463
We've only put our food down for the fifth bite.

00:17:44.463 --> 00:17:45.998
Then everyone else has finished eating.

00:17:45.998 --> 00:17:47.299
It's so nice to have a cafeteria here.

00:17:47.299 --> 00:17:48.534
Everyone finished eating in 15 minutes.

00:17:48.534 --> 00:17:49.902
The auntie is so happy.

00:17:49.902 --> 00:17:51.136
We're full now.

00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:52.638
The Korean lady said she would

00:17:52.638 --> 00:17:54.540
take us to see their headquarters.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:55.541
There's a showroom,

00:17:55.541 --> 00:17:56.742
so we walked there.

00:18:00.579 --> 00:18:02.281
It's a Korean electronic lock company.

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:03.482
Since you've come to the factory,

00:18:03.482 --> 00:18:05.117
you'll inevitably have to come to their headquarters.

00:18:05.117 --> 00:18:07.252
Since we've come to the birthplace of electronic locks, let's have

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:08.654
a display to show you

00:18:08.654 --> 00:18:10.222
the various types

00:18:10.222 --> 00:18:12.558
and features of electronic locks.

00:18:12.558 --> 00:18:13.826
First, look here.

00:18:13.826 --> 00:18:15.327
Cut across from this line in the middle

00:18:15.327 --> 00:18:16.795
and look

00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:18.931
this way. This is actually all Korean domestic sales.

00:18:18.931 --> 00:18:20.566
So you see

00:18:20.566 --> 00:18:22.968
the English name SOLITY written here

00:18:22.968 --> 00:18:25.571
. It's actually the Korean domestic sales brand

00:18:25.571 --> 00:18:26.939
, which is the

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:28.207
Korean pronunciation of

00:18:28.207 --> 00:18:29.374
this company.

00:18:29.374 --> 00:18:30.509
SOLITY

00:18:30.509 --> 00:18:31.743
. But everyone will surely think of

00:18:31.743 --> 00:18:33.712
the traditional

00:18:33.712 --> 00:18:34.947
locks we used to make ,

00:18:34.947 --> 00:18:36.548
especially those large locks for luxury homes, right?

00:18:36.548 --> 00:18:37.783
They had a row of

00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:38.517
buttons on top, which

00:18:38.517 --> 00:18:39.918
was very complicated . But if you look at this,

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:41.887
you'll see that in South Korea,

00:18:41.887 --> 00:18:43.288
the birthplace of electronic lock masters

00:18:43.288 --> 00:18:44.957
, their locks are so simple.

00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:46.091
The bolt is

00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:47.860
just a small section like this.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.094
Do you know what the biggest difference is?

00:18:49.094 --> 00:18:51.029
Of course, it can be traced back to the mechanical principle and structure. Because it's

00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:52.297
more energy-efficient and less labor-intensive

00:18:52.297 --> 00:18:53.532
to move smaller things.

00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:55.767
And the biggest reason is that

00:18:55.767 --> 00:18:57.703
there are fewer people breaking into homes now. Furthermore

00:18:57.703 --> 00:18:59.037
, thieves these days

00:18:59.037 --> 00:19:00.172
usually lack skills;

00:19:00.172 --> 00:19:01.440
they can only pick

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.808
doors you've forgotten to lock,

00:19:02.808 --> 00:19:04.243
or climb in through windows.

00:19:04.243 --> 00:19:05.077
The kind of skill

00:19:05.077 --> 00:19:06.145
you need to unlock slowly

00:19:06.145 --> 00:19:07.679
is what truly matters. Those skilled

00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:08.680
locksmiths have all become

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.182
thieves; why bother? Things

00:19:10.182 --> 00:19:11.283
have become more about

00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:12.818
protecting honest people from dishonest ones.

00:19:12.818 --> 00:19:13.652
People don't keep

00:19:13.652 --> 00:19:15.521
much gold or cash

00:19:15.521 --> 00:19:16.522
at home anymore.

00:19:16.522 --> 00:19:18.223
Those who want to steal large sums of money

00:19:18.223 --> 00:19:19.892
are now resorting to fraud.

00:19:19.892 --> 00:19:21.460
The worst kind of

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.761
fraudsters have

00:19:22.761 --> 00:19:23.795
no skills or

00:19:23.795 --> 00:19:24.930
expertise , so

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.365
learning lock picking would be better

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:28.567
. Therefore, prisons should teach people lock picking

00:19:28.567 --> 00:19:30.936
instead of fraud; they should teach them to steal.

00:19:30.936 --> 00:19:32.971
We can lie to them and say... You can steal more things,

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:34.673
and then I'll teach you how to

00:19:34.673 --> 00:19:36.408
pick locks. After learning how to pick locks, you'll find

00:19:36.408 --> 00:19:38.911
that you can make more money

00:19:38.911 --> 00:19:40.212
by picking locks for people who have forgotten their keys

00:19:40.212 --> 00:19:40.979
at night. You

00:19:40.979 --> 00:19:42.481
'll also see the police and not be afraid. It's

00:19:42.481 --> 00:19:43.482
a legitimate business

00:19:43.815 --> 00:19:44.783
. When you're outside,

00:19:44.783 --> 00:19:45.517
you'll help people open doors,

00:19:45.517 --> 00:19:46.485
but they

00:19:46.485 --> 00:19:48.921
still can't open your electronic lock.

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:50.122
This is for export.

00:19:50.122 --> 00:19:50.756
In Japan,

00:19:50.756 --> 00:19:52.658
they have some horizontal bar locks,

00:19:52.658 --> 00:19:53.959
and this one is exported to the US.

00:19:53.959 --> 00:19:55.460
But do you know why American locks are

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.295
sold? People might think that

00:19:56.295 --> 00:19:58.063
the US has a worse security situation

00:19:58.063 --> 00:19:59.731
, but why do American locks only use one lock?

00:19:59.731 --> 00:20:01.033
Because installing more won't

00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:02.701
help. People will still

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:03.535
break it. They'll break it.

00:20:03.535 --> 00:20:04.770
They'll dismantle the whole door.

00:20:05.804 --> 00:20:07.206
But you'll see

00:20:07.206 --> 00:20:08.507
that the structure and the way the American lock is drilled

00:20:08.507 --> 00:20:10.475
are actually very simple.

00:20:10.475 --> 00:20:11.243
In the US,

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:13.445
the wages

00:20:13.445 --> 00:20:15.547
are extremely high. If you go there, just for site inspection

00:20:15.547 --> 00:20:16.548
and nothing else,

00:20:16.548 --> 00:20:18.550
you might spend 5,000 or 6,000 NT dollars.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.086
So almost everyone there does their own installation

00:20:21.086 --> 00:20:22.554
. In Korea

00:20:22.554 --> 00:20:24.289
, many people can also do

00:20:24.289 --> 00:20:24.990
it themselves.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.225
So you see, in Korea,

00:20:26.225 --> 00:20:27.926
everyone's specifications are actually the same.

00:20:27.926 --> 00:20:28.760
There's the Korean standard,

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.695
the Japanese

00:20:29.695 --> 00:20:30.295
standard, and

00:20:30.295 --> 00:20:30.996
the American standard.

00:20:30.996 --> 00:20:32.197
Of course, there's also an American standard.

00:20:32.197 --> 00:20:33.699
Taiwan is the most special.

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:35.033
Taiwan doesn't have a Taiwanese standard.

00:20:35.033 --> 00:20:36.268
Taiwan's doors have

00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:38.870
Japanese, Korean, American, and European/American standards.

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:40.539
So many people

00:20:40.539 --> 00:20:41.540
are worried about whether

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.942
electronic locks can be installed in their homes.

00:20:43.942 --> 00:20:45.677
There's a simple way to check

00:20:45.677 --> 00:20:47.346
: just look at the thickness

00:20:47.346 --> 00:20:48.380
of the core. If it's

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.148
thin, it's generally fine.

00:20:50.148 --> 00:20:52.351
In Taiwan, there are old doors (30-40 years old)

00:20:52.351 --> 00:20:53.352
and old brass doors

00:20:53.352 --> 00:20:54.253
that are very thin

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:56.154
, or even thick doors in luxury homes

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:58.156
. The locks that are easy to install are those that can fit

00:20:58.156 --> 00:20:59.625
both thin and thick doors

00:20:59.625 --> 00:21:01.827
. That's why we filmed this company

00:21:01.827 --> 00:21:04.329
– because they can install locks

00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:07.132
of almost all kinds of odd and unusual sizes in Taiwan.

00:21:07.132 --> 00:21:07.766
Otherwise,

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:08.300
it's

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:09.501
useless if

00:21:09.501 --> 00:21:10.669
the lock can't be installed,

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:11.903
but it's

00:21:11.903 --> 00:21:12.871
too difficult to install it yourself. If you can

00:21:12.871 --> 00:21:13.872
install it yourself, why not?

00:21:13.872 --> 00:21:14.806
I can do it

00:21:14.806 --> 00:21:15.641
! It's your problem

00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:17.609
that you can't install it.

00:21:17.609 --> 00:21:18.543
Actually,

00:21:18.543 --> 00:21:20.345
electronic locks are divided into several types.

00:21:20.345 --> 00:21:21.213
The first type

00:21:21.213 --> 00:21:23.048
is the kind you used to see in Korean dramas,

00:21:23.048 --> 00:21:24.149
which is a button type.

00:21:24.149 --> 00:21:26.518
It's similar to a traditional home telephone.

00:21:26.518 --> 00:21:27.819
This type is

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:28.787
more intuitive for

00:21:28.787 --> 00:21:30.289
the elderly and children . You might prefer touch control

00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:32.190
, which uses a combination lock.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:32.991
Another type

00:21:32.991 --> 00:21:33.759
is card-based,

00:21:33.759 --> 00:21:34.493
like the

00:21:34.493 --> 00:21:35.594
MRT card, EasyCard, or

00:21:35.594 --> 00:21:37.596
RFID.

00:21:37.596 --> 00:21:38.563
You just use the card

00:21:38.563 --> 00:21:40.132
and beep to set it up.

00:21:40.132 --> 00:21:41.266
The third type

00:21:41.266 --> 00:21:42.301
is fingerprint.

00:21:42.301 --> 00:21:43.502
You press your

00:21:43.502 --> 00:21:45.337
fingerprint in and it identifies it.

00:21:45.337 --> 00:21:46.204
It says "

00:21:46.204 --> 00:21:47.539
Unregistered fingerprint."

00:21:47.539 --> 00:21:48.340
I'll listen again.

00:21:50.642 --> 00:21:53.945
Unregistered fingerprint.

00:21:53.945 --> 00:21:55.414
Actually, there's a problem with fingerprints.

00:21:55.414 --> 00:21:56.481
For example, you see...

00:21:56.481 --> 00:21:58.183
Before I came to Korea, if

00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.918
you were ever hurt or damaged

00:21:59.918 --> 00:22:01.386
at work, you

00:22:01.386 --> 00:22:02.954
might feel very embarrassed and suddenly find yourself unable to get into your own home.

00:22:02.954 --> 00:22:03.622
I suggest

00:22:03.622 --> 00:22:05.324
you try using different fingers

00:22:05.324 --> 00:22:06.425
and setting

00:22:06.425 --> 00:22:08.660
different angles for each finger,

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.495
just in case you can't get in.

00:22:10.495 --> 00:22:11.763
Another type is the

00:22:11.763 --> 00:22:13.398
facial recognition system

00:22:13.398 --> 00:22:15.600
, where you scan your face to enter.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:17.536
Some also have buttons

00:22:17.536 --> 00:22:18.437
or passwords,

00:22:18.437 --> 00:22:20.272
and some use RFID

00:22:20.272 --> 00:22:21.540
, which is card-based.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:22.874
But sometimes it has evolved into a system

00:22:22.874 --> 00:22:25.911
where facial recognition scans your face to see

00:22:25.911 --> 00:22:26.945
if you can get in.

00:22:26.945 --> 00:22:28.547
Sometimes twins have

00:22:28.547 --> 00:22:30.048
even been found to be able to enter each other's homes.

00:22:30.048 --> 00:22:32.551
There was also an experiment online that

00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:34.653
... If you print a photo of a person

00:22:34.653 --> 00:22:36.254
and place it on the screen

00:22:36.254 --> 00:22:37.522
, and the door opens,

00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:38.323
it's fake.

00:22:38.323 --> 00:22:39.157
That's

00:22:39.157 --> 00:22:40.225
impossible; the photo

00:22:40.225 --> 00:22:41.893
is fake . Or, the person might be drunk,

00:22:41.893 --> 00:22:43.562
and a friend might carry them to their doorstep

00:22:43.562 --> 00:22:45.564
and lift their face like that.

00:22:45.564 --> 00:22:46.498
That's possible

00:22:46.498 --> 00:22:46.932
, of course

00:22:46.932 --> 00:22:48.633
. So basically, as long as the face is the person's,

00:22:48.633 --> 00:22:49.568
regardless of whether they're drunk

00:22:49.568 --> 00:22:50.135
, sober

00:22:50.135 --> 00:22:51.169
, or unconscious

00:22:51.169 --> 00:22:53.171
, as long as you can grab the person's head

00:22:53.171 --> 00:22:55.140
and scan the camera,

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:56.842
it can generally open the door.

00:22:56.842 --> 00:22:57.709
But you might be thinking, what

00:22:57.709 --> 00:22:58.910
if I scan my face

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:01.713
, 3D print my head

00:23:01.713 --> 00:23:03.915
, or use silicone molding

00:23:03.915 --> 00:23:05.150
to create a

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:06.685
mask of myself?

00:23:06.685 --> 00:23:07.652
That's basically impossible

00:23:07.652 --> 00:23:08.987
because the camera

00:23:08.987 --> 00:23:10.288
doesn't scan flat. The surface

00:23:10.288 --> 00:23:12.758
is actually three-dimensional, corresponding to the position,

00:23:12.758 --> 00:23:14.493
and there's infrared light to

00:23:14.493 --> 00:23:15.527
scan your blood,

00:23:15.527 --> 00:23:16.795
whether your pupils are blinking

00:23:16.795 --> 00:23:18.163
, or your

00:23:19.931 --> 00:23:21.166
breathing dynamics.

00:23:21.166 --> 00:23:22.734
It scans a lot of things.

00:23:22.734 --> 00:23:23.702
But before this,

00:23:23.702 --> 00:23:26.905
we filmed several different lock

00:23:26.905 --> 00:23:28.507
videos or posts

00:23:28.507 --> 00:23:30.175
, and everyone had the same question:

00:23:30.175 --> 00:23:31.076
What if I'm in Taiwan

00:23:31.076 --> 00:23:32.511
and suddenly go abroad for a long time

00:23:32.511 --> 00:23:34.179
and come back to Taiwan with an electronic lock

00:23:34.179 --> 00:23:35.380
that runs out of power?

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:36.047
It's simple, just

00:23:36.047 --> 00:23:37.682
go to a convenience store to buy batteries.

00:23:37.682 --> 00:23:38.450
There aren't many

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:39.284
convenience stores in Taiwan; at most

00:23:39.284 --> 00:23:40.118
, you go to a convenience store

00:23:40.118 --> 00:23:41.420
and buy an AA battery

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:42.354
. We'll

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:43.355
say

00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:44.222
AA battery

00:23:44.222 --> 00:23:45.557
, or even just a

00:23:45.557 --> 00:23:47.292
5 -size battery

00:23:47.292 --> 00:23:48.326
. Which one is it?

00:23:48.326 --> 00:23:49.428
Think carefully before answering.

00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:50.862
For example ,

00:23:50.862 --> 00:23:52.898
if this has two 'A's,

00:23:52.898 --> 00:23:55.967
it's called a '3' battery in Taiwan. In

00:23:55.967 --> 00:23:58.904
South Korea and mainland China, it's called a '5' battery.

00:23:58.904 --> 00:24:00.105
The smaller one

00:24:00.105 --> 00:24:01.306
is called a '4' battery.

00:24:01.306 --> 00:24:03.708
But in South Korea and mainland China,

00:24:03.708 --> 00:24:05.677
they call a '7' battery (three 'A's).

00:24:05.677 --> 00:24:06.445
It's complicated

00:24:06.445 --> 00:24:07.412
, and you don't need to know.

00:24:07.412 --> 00:24:09.381
If you need to replace the battery,

00:24:09.381 --> 00:24:11.116
it's in the back

00:24:11.116 --> 00:24:12.417
of the indoor unit.

00:24:12.417 --> 00:24:14.453
But if

00:24:14.453 --> 00:24:16.521
I 'm outside

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:18.690
and need emergency power,

00:24:18.690 --> 00:24:20.158
the product has two

00:24:20.158 --> 00:24:22.260
battery terminals

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:24.696
that can supply 9V batteries.

00:24:24.696 --> 00:24:27.098
You need to plug the battery into these

00:24:27.098 --> 00:24:29.167
